`Low` - `PKSampler.num_batches=max(1, ...)` avoids zero-batch dry-runs, but very small `--limit_train` can still produce fewer than `P` identities and therefore a non-64 dry-run batch at [scripts/exp324b_train_head.py](/Users/abdslm/Desktop/SOLIDER-REID/scripts/exp324b_train_head.py:254). Full training is unaffected with the real train set.

Verified: part-loss shapes and `vmask` are correct; param-group split is correct; `scheduler.step()` is placed after epoch optimizer steps; all `step()` consumers expect 7 values; triplet, part-MaxSim eval, heavy-query slicing, and same-pid/same-cam exclusion remain intact. I did not execute a dry-run here because this environment is read-only/no GPU.
